---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../data/site";

const title = "Privacy Policy";
const description = "Read how Echo Buddha handles analytics, cookies, advertising technologies, email messages, and privacy choices.";
const canonicalPath = "/privacy-policy/";
const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "PrivacyPolicy",
  name: title,
  description,
  url: `${SITE.url}${canonicalPath}`,
  publisher: {
    "@type": "Organization",
    name: SITE.name,
    url: SITE.url,
    email: SITE.email
  }
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath={canonicalPath} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Policy</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Last updated: August 6, 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p>
        Echo Buddha is an educational website. This policy explains the types of information that may be collected
        when visitors use the site and how future services may affect privacy.
      </p>
      <h2>Cookies and Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Echo Buddha uses Google Analytics only after you choose to accept optional analytics. Until then, the site does
        not load the Google Analytics script or send standard analytics page-view events. If accepted, Google Analytics
        may use cookies or related technologies to understand general website usage, such as page views, approximate
        device information, and navigation patterns.
      </p>
      <p>
        Analytics information is reviewed in aggregate where possible. Echo Buddha uses it to understand which pages are
        useful, identify technical issues, and improve navigation, search, and reading experience. Analytics consent is
        separate from advertising consent, and accepting analytics does not enable advertising personalization.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your analytics choice is stored in a first-party preference named <code>echo_buddha_privacy_consent</code> so the
        site can remember whether you accepted or rejected optional analytics. You can reopen privacy settings from the
        footer or the button below, and you can withdraw analytics consent at any time.
      </p>
      <button class="button button--secondary" type="button" data-privacy-settings>Manage privacy settings</button>
      <h2>Advertising and Google AdSense</h2>
      <p>
        Echo Buddha may load the Google AdSense publisher script on the homepage for site verification and on a limited
        set of article and learning pages. The script is not intentionally loaded on search, error, tools, policy, trust,
        quote, daily reflection, meditation, source-study, dictionary, or sensitive wellbeing pages.
      </p>
      <p>
        Manual ad units are not currently used. If manual ad placements are introduced later, they should appear only as
        clearly labeled Advertisement areas and should stay away from meditation instructions, safety notes, quote text,
        navigation, buttons, tools, and other sensitive page elements.
      </p>
      <p>
        Visitors can learn about or manage Google ad personalization through
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>. Additional choices
        may be available through browser settings or regional consent tools.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact and Email</h2>
      <p>
        If you contact Echo Buddha by email, your message and email address may be used to respond to your inquiry.
        Email messages are not sold or used to create public profiles.
      </p>
      <h2>Third-Party Links</h2>
      <p>
        Articles may link to external resources. Echo Buddha is not responsible for the privacy practices of
        third-party websites.
      </p>
      <h2>Your Choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can restrict or delete cookies through browser controls. Blocking some technologies may affect website
        features or measurement. Echo Buddha also provides a privacy settings control in the footer for optional
        analytics. Where legally required, additional consent choices may be needed before non-essential cookies are
        used. This policy is an engineering and transparency statement, not legal advice; jurisdiction-specific legal
        adequacy may require qualified review.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be sent to
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
